<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>BabyLM task scores for the four models from <a href="#S3.F2" title="In Experimental setup ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Once Upon a Time:Interactive Learning for Storytelling with Small Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Accuracy metrics are reported as percentages, WUG-A/P as Spearman’s <math id="A6.T8.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, AoA as Pearson’s <math id="A6.T8.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, Eye-T and SPR as partial correlations <math id="A6.T8.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{p}R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{p}R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Bold indicates the best model for each task.</figcaption>
</figure>
